    "result_text": "The change is implemented and the test suite passes (`BUILD SUCCESS`, `Tests run: 1, Failures: 0, Errors: 0`).\n\n## What I did\n\nThe `customerCode` is built in `generateCustomerCode(...)` in `OwnerRestControllerV1.java` as `<REGION>-<HASH8>`. Previously this was a pure deterministic derivation, so two distinct owners sharing the same region, normalized telephone, and last name would collide.\n\nI added a de-duplication step there (`OwnerRestControllerV1.java:558`):\n\n1. Compute the base code (`region + \"-\" + hash8`) as before.\n2. Collect the `customerCode` of every existing owner into a `Set` (filtering out nulls).\n3. If the base code is unused, return it unchanged.\n4. Otherwise append `-<n>`, picking the smallest `n \u2265 2` that is not already in use, and return that.\n\nThis follows the same `clinicService.findAllOwners().stream()` collision-check idiom already used by the surrounding `rejectDuplicateIdentity` / `rejectHouseholdDuplicate` helpers. I also added the `java.util.stream.Collectors` import and updated the method's Javadoc to document the de-duplication guarantee.\n\nThe new `AcceptanceTest.coreCustomerCodesStayUnique` and the rest of the suite pass.",
