    "final_verdict": "VERDICT: LGTM\n\nThe de-duplication logic is placed and shaped consistently with the surrounding code:\n\n- This controller already keeps a family of private owner-derivation/validation helpers (`normalizeEmail`, `countNamesakes`, `generateCustomerCode`, `regionForPostcode`), so extending `generateCustomerCode` to produce the *final* customer code is the natural home for this logic \u2014 the spec is literally \"return the de-duplicated customerCode.\"\n- Querying `this.clinicService.findAllOwners().stream()` from a private controller helper is the established idiom here \u2014 `countNamesakes` (line 535) does the exact same thing. So the change is additive and matches the house style rather than introducing a new access pattern.\n- The method stays cohesive: it builds one value (the customer code) and the collision suffix is part of producing that value, not a separate concern worth its own unit.\n- The javadoc was updated accurately (including the `@return` and a clear paragraph on the `-<n>` rule), keeping documentation in step with behavior.\n\nNo duplication, no catch-all growth, and a maintainer of this file would find it natural.",
